I've thrown food rations (may have been a C-ration or a K-ration) to a pet and it's been
eaten before. They don't eat bad food though, or tins, but if the "pet" is wild, it will
stop attacking you - even if you throw tins - useful if you want to keep your options open.
That's not to say the pet becomes tame if it doesn't eat the food (it behaves like a
"friendly" monster would), so I'd guess (tho' I haven't tried this) that you can't train a
pet by throwing the same tin (or whatever) at it repeatedly. Anyone know?

